  "_provenance": {
    "policy": "Snapshots record list price only — never promotional, introductory, or time-limited pricing. A model on a temporary discount or an upcoming price increase is still recorded at its current post-introductory list price. Where an entry deviates from its source for this reason, the deviation is stated in that entry's 'note'.",
    "attribution": "Entries are imported from a third-party, MIT-licensed, community-maintained model-pricing dataset. Portions Copyright (c) 2023 Berri AI; used under the MIT License. MIT requires the permission notice and warranty disclaimer to travel with the copyright line, so the full licence text is reproduced in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md at the crate root — that file must accompany any redistribution of this data or of a binary built with it.",
    "revision": "Entries carrying verified_on 2026-08-07, 2026-09-01 or 2026-09-03 were imported from that dataset at commit b45b4b73004261b47369d7d12c97d58b137a732e, so this refresh can be re-run and diffed against the same input. The 2026-09-01 and 2026-09-03 entries were re-derived at that same pinned commit rather than at the newest one: they were re-imported to correct cache multipliers, and re-deriving them at a later revision would have folded an unrelated price refresh into that correction. Older entries predate revision pinning; their exact source commit was not recorded and cannot be recovered from this file alone.",
    "field_policy": "Every field — per-token pricing, context_window, max_output_tokens, and all multipliers — is carried from the source at the pinned revision. No field is inferred from a prior-generation sibling model, and a model absent from the source is not added from memory. Cache and batch multipliers are derived as ratios of the source's absolute costs; an omitted multiplier is billed at 1.0 by the cost engine, so a multiplier the source provides is always recorded.",
    "per_entry_fields": "Entries carry optional 'source' (where the figure was actually read: 'aggregated-dataset' for a direct import, a vendor host only where that page was itself fetched), 'verified_on' (ISO date the figure was taken from that source), 'note' (caveats a future reader would otherwise misread as an import error), and 'deprecation_notice' (vendor shutdown date and migration target). A 'source' with no 'verified_on' is a pre-pinning import: the origin is known, the date is not. Earlier revisions of this file spelled some of these with a leading underscore ('_source'); that spelling is retired — the leading underscore now marks file-level metadata only, so '_provenance' is the sole underscored key in the file."
  },
